  "pli-tv-bu-vb-np25:2.10": "The six are linen, cotton, silk, wool, sunn hemp, and hemp; see [pli-tv-kd8:3.1.6]().  According to [pli-tv-kd8:21.1.4](), the size referred to here  is no smaller than 8 by 4 _sugataṅgula_, “standard fingerbreadths”. For an explanation of the idea of _vikappanā_, see Appendix of Technical Terms. For the rendering of _cīvara_ as “robe-cloth”, see the same appendix. ",
